% // Not a map — there is no basemap to draw on. A plot of where these places
% // are in relation to each other, which is a different and smaller claim.
< section class="index-head"
  <p class="eyebrow">{{ req.count }} places the corpus can locate
  <h1>Places
  <p>Every article whose subject has coordinates, plotted against each other. There is no coastline behind them: this shows relative position and nothing more. Degrees {{ req.west }} to {{ req.east }} east, {{ req.south }} to {{ req.north }} north.

< div class="plot-wrap"
  < div class="plot"
    % for (const place of req.places) {
    < a class="pin" href="{{ place.url }}" style="left: {{ place.x }}%; top: {{ place.y }}%"
      <span class="pin-dot"
      <span class="pin-label">{{ place.title }}
    % }

< div class="page"
  < div class="prose"
    < table
      < thead
        < tr
          <th>Place
          <th>North
          <th>East
          <th>When
      < tbody
        % for (const place of req.places) {
        < tr
          <td>[[ {{ place.title }} | {{ place.url }} ]]
          <td>{{ place.lat }}
          <td>{{ place.lon }}
          <td>{{ place.when }}
        % }
